Address two verified review findings. In `JmxTelemetryTest.bundledAndCustomJvmSchemas`, enable `jvm.memory.init` first, then pass an empty unstable-metrics selector in the case where unstable metrics should be disabled. Keep the JVM system selected and retain the assertions that the bundled unstable metric is absent while the custom metric with the same name remains. The regression should fail if the setter ignores an empty selector instead of resetting it.

Add a short entry under the Unreleased breaking changes in `CHANGELOG.md` explaining that an explicitly empty selector now selects nothing for `setInternalMetricsSystemFilter` and `setInternalMetricsUnstableMetricsFilter`, and that callers can use `IncludeExclude.builder().setIncluded("*").build()` to keep the previous select-all behavior. The user explicitly requested no `breaking change` label; do not add or request one. Preserve the existing production code and defaults-first README. Keep the changes scoped to the test and changelog, and run the focused JMX library test and repository Markdown formatter if feasible.

